    "question": "Harly's animal shelter has 80 dogs. She adopts out 40% of them but then has to take back 5 because of personality conflicts with other dogs in their adopted homes. How many dogs does she have now?",
    "gold": "53",
    "answer": "First find how many dogs are adopted out: 80 dogs * 40% = <<80*40*.01=32>>32 dogs\nThen subtract the number of dogs adopted out from the total number of dogs and add the number who were returned to find the final number of dogs: 80 dogs - 32 dogs + 5 dogs = <<80-32+5=53>>53 dogs\n#### 53"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many dogs Harly's animal shelter has after the adoption and return process, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of dogs adopted out.\n2. Subtract the number of adopted dogs from the initial number of dogs.\n3. Add the number of dogs returned to the shelter.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the number of dogs adopted out.\nHarly adopts out 40% of the 80 dogs.\n\\[ 40\\% \\text{ of } 80 = 0.40 \\times 80 = 32 \\]\nSo, 32 dogs are adopted out.\n\nStep 2: Subtract the number of adopted dogs from the initial number of dogs.\n\\[ 80 - 32 = 48 \\]\nSo, after adopting out 32 dogs, there are 48 dogs left.\n\nStep 3: Add the number of dogs returned to the shelter.\nHarly has to take back 5 dogs due to personality conflicts.\n\\[ 48 + 5 = 53 \\]\nSo, after taking back 5 dogs, there are 53 dogs in the shelter.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{53}\n\\]",
